{"name":"Deepsea Kraken","hex":"#082599","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deepsea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of deep-sea."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deepsea"},{"term":"kraken","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of Kraken."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kraken"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kraken","blocks":[{"text":"The kraken is a legendary cryptid of enormous size, per its etymology something akin to a cephalopod, said to appear in the Norwegian Sea off the coast of Norway. It is believed that the legend of the Kraken may have originated from sightings of giant squid, which may grow to 10.5 metres (34 ft) in length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Le_Poulpe_Colossal.jpg/330px-Le_Poulpe_Colossal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kraken","wikidata":"Q193165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Naturalistslibra25-p326a-kraken.jpg/500px-Naturalistslibra25-p326a-kraken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Naturalistslibra25-p326a-kraken.jpg/500px-Naturalistslibra25-p326a-kraken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kraken, an unconfirmed cephalopod.[a] Engraving by W. H. Lizars, in Hamilton, Robert (1839). Naturalist's Library. Adapted \"from Denys Montford\" [sic.][5]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANaturalistslibra25-p326a-kraken.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Krake_%28tr%C3%A4dragg%29.jpg/500px-Krake_%28tr%C3%A4dragg%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Krake_%28tr%C3%A4dragg